      "name": "EQ-BioDT: Empty Quarter Biodiversity Digital Twin",
      "description": "Biodiversity Digital Twin for the Rub' al Khali (Empty Quarter) hyperarid desert ecosystem. Integrates a 1,043 km multi-campaign spatiotemporal data cube (60 primary + 10 auxiliary sites, 2,550 specimens, 573 shotgun libraries, 5,438 dereplicated species-level MAGs [756 high-quality], 19,300 vOTUs, 322,755 pOTUs, 33 XRF analytes, CaCl2 pH, and collection-date-matched ERA5/NASA POWER hydroclimate) with a Two-Layer Causal-Ontological Engine (OCS = 1.0) and European BioDT/B-Cubed/LTER-LIFE/DTO-BioFlow standards for environmental management via cloud seeding, revegetation, desalination/brine governance, subsurface refugium protection, megafauna reintroduction (Oryx/Gazelle vs Camel grazing), and seismic/hydrocarbon bioremediation.",
      "license": { "@id": "https://spdx.org/licenses/MIT.html" },
